  "description": "T1 Large Robinia (Robinia pseudoacacia)Carry out a crown reduction of the Large Robinia, reducing the overall height by approximately 2.5 metres back to suitable growth pointsthroughout the crown.Works shall also include the removal of all dead, dying and diseased branchwood throughout the canopy. Pruning shall be undertakenselectively to maintain the tree's natural form, balance and healthy furnishing growth whilst reducing end-weight and improving long-termcrown structure.T2 Bay (Laurus nobilis)Carry out a crown reduction of the Bay tree, reducing the overall height by approximately 2.5 metres and reshaping to create a balanced,symmetrical and well-proportioned specimen. Works shall be undertaken by pruning back to suitable growth points whilst maintaining healthyfoliage cover and the tree's natural character.T3 Silver Birch (Betula pendula)Carry out a crown reduction of the Silver Birch, reducing the overall height by approximately 2.0 metres back to suitable growth pointsthroughout the upper crown. Works shall be undertaken selectively to retain the tree's natural form, structural integrity and healthy furnishinggrowth.T4 Fig (Ficus carica)Carry out a crown reduction by removing all new growth back to the previous points of reduction, reinstating the established crown framework.&nbsp;Works shall be undertaken selectively throughout the canopy to maintain the tree's natural form whilst encouraging healthy future growth.T5 Large Olive (Olea europaea)Carry out a crown reduction of the Large Olive, reducing the overall height by approximately 1.5 metres and reshaping the crown to create abalanced and well-proportioned specimen. Works shall be undertaken selectively, pruning back to suitable growth points whilst maintainingthe natural habit and healthy foliage cover of the tree.T6 Olive (Olea europaea)Carry out a crown reduction of the Olive tree, reducing the overall height by approximately 1.0 metre and reshaping to create a neat, balancedand symmetrical crown. Works shall be undertaken to suitable growth points whilst maintaining the tree's natural form and long term health.T7 Buddleia (Buddleja davidii)Carefully fell the Buddleia to ground level. All arisings shall be removed from site and disposed of responsibly, leaving the area clear and tidy.All works shall be carried out in accordance with BS39982010 - Tree Work RecommendationsReason for works:General tree maintenance",
